   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Solve each equation for x: \\( x = 2 y^{2} - 1 \\) from the graph of p, with \\( y \\ge 0 \\), and \\( x = 3 y + 8 \\) from the graph of q.",
         "rule_named": "rewrite each curve as a function of y"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The curves meet where \\( 2 y^{2} - 1 = 3 y + 8 \\), at \\( y = 3 \\), and the region runs from the x-axis, \\( y = 0 \\), up to there. On that interval the line is to the right of the parabola.",
         "rule_named": "limits in y and the right-hand curve"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The area is \\( \\int_{0}^{3} \\left(\\left(3 y + 8\\right) - \\left(2 y^{2} - 1\\right)\\right)\\,dy = \\frac{45}{2} \\).",
